  "title": "Reference images become a workflow",
  "summary": "September expanded image-making and model choices while giving people clearer ways to use, track, and build on Pollinations.\n\nNano Banana and Seedream 4.0 added image generation from reference URLs. The image editor gained support for up to four references on compatible models, and Enter added listings for both models.\n\nGitHub sign-in, self-service API keys, and a Pollen balance view gave Enter an account workflow. Free registered services can be called without a key; paid requests gained session and balance checks, usage pricing, and tracking.\n\nThe text lineup shifted through several mappings before `openai` settled on GPT-5 Mini and `openai-fast` on GPT-5 Nano. Gemini Search added a search-grounded route, while model definitions took on more of the routing and request behavior.\n\nThe project directories grew with image generators, collaborative comics, multilingual chat and teaching tools, a VS Code extension, and community-built developer tools. The listings also distinguished the official MCP server from a community-maintained one.",
